    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0425" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg355"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 23, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The receipt of despatches Nos. 161 and 162
                    is hereby acknowledged.</p>
                <p>Despatch No. 161 was accompanied by memoranda explanatory of the proceedings of
                    the government in reference to certain difficulties existing between Major
                    General Butler and the foreign consuls at New Orleans.</p>
                <p>It is only necessary to add that, believing it might be of importance to apprise
                    this government at once of the conciliatory action initiated by the government
                    of the United States, I forthwith submitted the memoranda in question to Mr.
                    Thouvenel to be read. He returned it with his thanks, informing <pb facs="0426"
                        n="356" xml:id="pg356"/> me, however, that the text had already been
                    received from his Majesty’s minister at Washington.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi><hi
                            rendition="#italic"> Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
